# oracle: w314gm_lj_tri — w246gm_lj_gibbs in triclinic boxes (xy 0.3, xz 0.2, yz 0.1 in units of the cell): the volume change keeps the tilt factors, and an inserted atom is a uniform point in lamda coordinates
# oracle-partitions: 2
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.1e-15, atoms 1.0e-12 (an exchange into the gas box at cycle 3 and one back by cycle 21).
variable temp index 1.0
variable ntranslate index 10
variable nexchange index 10
variable nvolume index 10
variable displace index 0.5
variable max_dlogvolratio index 0.5
variable nsteps index 30
units lj
atom_style atomic
variable rho world 0.05 0.6
variable ncell world 1 2
lattice fcc ${rho}
region box block 0 ${ncell} 0 ${ncell} 0 ${ncell}
create_box 1 box
create_atoms 1 box
change_box all triclinic xy final 0.3 xz final 0.2 yz final 0.1 remap units lattice
mass 1 1.0
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor 0.3 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 5 check yes
fix 2 all gemc 1 ${ntranslate} ${nexchange} ${nvolume} ${temp} ${displace} ${max_dlogvolratio} 29494
thermo 1
thermo_style custom step pe vol atoms
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run ${nsteps}
